---
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import FaqItem from '../components/FaqItem.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Poker Assistant FAQ" description="Free heads-up GTO, one-time packs, local hand analysis, supported sites and platforms - answered clearly.">
  <PageHeader marker="FAQ" title="Straight answers before you start" lede="Free means free. Local means local. Here is what Poker Assistant does and does not do." />
  <Section top="sm" bottom="2xl" width="content">
    <Faq>
      <FaqItem question="Do my hands ever leave my device?" open><p>No. Hand histories, practice results and study data stay on your tablet or Mac. No account. No cloud. No uploads.</p></FaqItem>
      <FaqItem question="Which sites can I import from?"><p>PokerStars, GGPoker, 888poker, Winamax and iPoker. Paste a hand, open a file, or on macOS import a whole history folder. Poker Assistant detects the site automatically.</p></FaqItem>
      <FaqItem question="What is free, exactly?"><p>The app and every heads-up solution: 8bb to 200bb, including ante, rake and straddle structures. The trainer, hand import, node locking and preflop builder have no daily cap.</p></FaqItem>
      <FaqItem question="Will heads-up stay free?"><p>Yes. Heads-up is a permanent part of Poker Assistant: no expiry, no subscription and no limit.</p></FaqItem>
      <FaqItem question="What do packs cost?"><p>Prices arrive at launch. Every pack is a one-time purchase. Never a monthly fee.</p></FaqItem>
      <FaqItem question="What happens to a pack after I buy it?"><p>It is yours. Restore it after a reinstall or on a new device without paying again. New coverage is optional; the solutions you bought remain available.</p></FaqItem>
      <FaqItem question="Which table sizes and stack depths are solved?"><p>From heads-up to 9-handed. The raise ladder runs from 15bb to 200bb; push/fold covers 8bb, 10bb and 12bb. See the <a href="/solutions">full coverage</a>.</p></FaqItem>
      <FaqItem question="Is it solved for my rake?"><p>Yes, where the pack matches your game. Rake packs use 5% capped at 3bb; ante packs use 0.125bb and 0.5bb antes; straddle packs use a 2bb straddle. Each is solved separately because each changes the strategy.</p></FaqItem>
      <FaqItem question="Can I use it while I play?"><p>No. Poker Assistant is for study away from the table. Real-time assistance breaks major poker sites' rules and can cost you your account.</p></FaqItem>
      <FaqItem question="Which platforms, and when?"><p>iPadOS, macOS and Android. Poker Assistant has not shipped yet; the site will announce each release.</p></FaqItem>
      <FaqItem question="Does it do tournaments and ICM?"><p>Not yet. Current solutions use chip EV for cash games, early tournament stages and winner-take-all formats. Bubble and final-table ICM are not included.</p></FaqItem>
      <FaqItem question="Can I solve my own spots?"><p>Yes. Set the stacks, open size and structure, then run a preflop solve on your device. From that line, solve any flop through the turn and river.</p></FaqItem>
      <FaqItem question="How is this different from cloud study tools?"><p>Your data stays local, complete heads-up coverage is free, and packs are yours after one purchase. The <a href="/accuracy">accuracy page</a> shows how the solves are measured.</p></FaqItem>
    </Faq>
    {/* Held until the owner decides them (spec section 2): */}
    {/* Who makes it? */}
    {/* Can I move my data to a new phone? */}
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
